-------------------
Maintained

Automatic Recovery:
-------------------
Occurs When Superior BPDUs Stop

Summary
=======

Problem:
A rogue or misconfigured switch could advertise superior BPDUs and become the Root Bridge.

Solution:
Root Guard prevents downstream switches from taking over the Root Bridge role.

Benefit:
Maintains a stable STP topology and protects network design.

Limitation:
Does not protect against unidirectional link failures.

